Keyboard needs:
- KSCAN driver
  from ZephyrOS
  uses 'zmk,kscan-gpio-matrix' vs 'zmk,kscan-gpio-direct'
  Kscan -> keyboard scan
    Detect key press in a connected matrix keyboard OR any device with buttons
  API
    kscan_callback_t
    kscan_config
    kscan_enable_callback
- Optional matrix transform
  Defines how KSCAN row/column events are translated into
  logical 'key positions'
- keymap bind key position to <behavior> (key press mod-tap, momentary layer)

Self contained keyboard

Pin control
- Subsystem that manages multiplexing, configuration and control
  of pin functions
- GPIO focuses on basic IO operation, while PINCTRL deal with assigning and
  configuring pin functionality within the system.

- Microcontroller pins often have multiple possible functions (e.g., GPIO UART I2C SPI, PWM)
  PINCTRL allows selection of the function that the pin will perform
- Also also set drive strength slew rate, pull up pull down, IO mode

UDC - USB Device Controller

ble.c seems ok!

GATT (Generic Attribute Profiles)
- needs value, properties, and permissions
  Properties (bit value fields)
  - BT_GATT_CHRC_BROADCAST - allow broadcast of the VALUE
  - BT_GATT_CHRC_READ - allow READS of value
  - BT_GATT_CHRC_WRITE_WITHOUT_RESP - allow write of VALUE WITHOUT response
  - BT_GATT_CHRC_WRITE - allow write WITH response
  - BT_GATT_CHRC_NOTIFY - allow notification without ack
  - BT_GATT_CHRC_INDICATE - allow indications of value with acknowledgement
  - BT_GATT_CHRC_AUTH - allow signed writes to VALUE
- CCC (Client Characteristic Configuration) descsription for a Characteristic


Bluetooth EIR (Extended Inquiery Response)
- Refers to advertising data and scan response data that devies use to broadcast info about themselves

